# Implementation plans are local-only, ephemeral work artifacts (see docs/plans/README.md).
# They go stale the moment code merges; the durable "why" lives in docs/specs/ + docs/adrs/,
# and the durable "what happened" in docs/reports/. CI enforces this
# (scripts/check-no-committed-plans.sh) because this rule alone is advisory.
docs/plans/*
!docs/plans/README.md

# Claude Code local config. Keep this: in a sandboxed setup the launcher copies global
# settings -- which can carry tokens -- into the project's .claude/.
.claude/

# Secrets and credentials
.env
.env.*
.env.local
# The demo's own environment file. It holds a GitHub token (DEMO_GH_TOKEN) and an ntfy
# topic, which is itself a capability — anyone who learns it can read and publish your
# notifications. `scripts/login.py` deliberately writes nothing to disk; this file is
# what an operator assembles by hand so a fresh pane can source it.
.demo-env
.demo-llm-env
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
credentials.*
secrets.*
*kubeconfig*
# `kind_setup.py --kubeconfig .kube/config-kind` writes here by default, and the file
# carries client certificates. The `*kubeconfig*` glob above does NOT match it.
.kube/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Bogus lock file created by running uv outside the project directory.
uv.lock

# Never commit a credential used by the demo. The demo overlay references
# Secret/anthropic-credentials and scripts/k8s_deploy.py creates it from the
# environment at deploy time; these patterns catch a local file made by hand.
# (Inherited from rossoctl/examples, with the `eventing/` path prefix dropped.)
**/*seed*.hex
**/anthropic-credentials*.yaml
**/*.secret.yaml

# Local run artifacts: PID files and the SQLite event store.
*.pid
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
